  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The differential equation of the family of curves $y=e^{x}(A \\cos x+B \\sin x)$ where $A, B$ are arbitrary constants is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "S0Uea",
      "text": "$\\frac{d^{2} y}{d x^{2}}-9 x=13$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kwkk8",
      "text": "$\\frac{d^{2} y}{d x^{2}}-2 \\frac{d y}{d x}+2 y=0$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "RgG0o",
      "text": "$\\frac{d^{2} y}{d x^{2}}+3 y=4$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tFAHq",
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{d y}{d x}\\right)^{2}+\\frac{d y}{d x}-x y=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\n$y=e^{x}(A \\cos x+B \\sin x)$\r\nDifferentiating w.r.t. x:-\r\n$y^{\\prime}=y+e^{x}(-A \\sin x+B \\cos x)$\r\nDifferentiating w.r.t. $x$ once again:-\r\n$\\begin{array}{c}\r\ny^{\\prime \\prime}=y^{\\prime}+\\left(y^{\\prime}-y\\right)+e^{x}(-A \\cos x-B \\sin x) \\\\\r\n=2 y^{\\prime}-y-y \\quad \\Rightarrow y^{\\prime \\prime}-2 y^{\\prime}+2 y=0\r\n\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
